{
  "slug": "orchestra",
  "name": "Orchestra",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Disciplined AI engineering toolkit for Claude Code. Ships typed design-doc templates (Feature LLD, Bug Report, ADR, Postmortem, Runbook, Design Doc) with a 4-gate spec review (Completeness / Evidence / Clarity / Consistency), mandatory mermaid diagrams, an octal-safe auto-numbering script, AGENTS.md and llms.txt sync, a bug-iteration loop that prevents orphan fix-commits, and an enforced doc-before-code workflow with five named gates (Discovery / Design / Spec Review / Commit / Implementation Sync). Includes a Python lint CLI for Refs:-line + metadata + status validation, an auto DECISIONS.md generator with bidirectional ADR supersession consistency. Patterns adopted from Michael Nygard, Google SRE, Pragmatic Engineer, agents.md, and llmstxt.org. First skill of the Orchestra umbrella; future skills cover workflow, registry, tasks, gates, and plans.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 skills** and **1 command**.\n\n- **Skills** (4): `commit` (Commit-discipline skill — invoke before any code commit, any doc commit on canon-frozen-eligible file, status-flip operations, supersession decisions), `design-docs` (Use when a feature, bug fix, architectural decision, incident postmortem, operational runbook, or component-level architecture update needs a…), `init` (Use when setting up design docs scaffolding in a new repo, or when migrating from orchestra v1.0 to…), `spec-review` (Use when reviewing any orchestra design doc (Feature LLD, Bug Report, ADR, Postmortem, Runbook, Design Doc, Plan) via…)\n- **Commands** (1): `spec-review` (Run orchestra:spec-review v2 (6-parallel-sub-judge ensemble) on a doc — produces schema-v2.0 attestation)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install orchestra@claude-community` from `hassan-mohiddin/orchestra`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 4,
    "command": 1
  },
